  Node writes [38;5;153mJSON.stringify(record)[39m as one line per record (what log collectors want). The browser passes the record
  object to [38;5;153mconsole.debug/info/warn/error[39m so devtools keeps it inspectable. Same data, format suited to each reader.

  [1m6. The transport seam[0m

  [38;5;153msetSink(fn)[39m registers one function, called with the finished, already-redacted record after console output. A throwing
  sink is caught and swallowed — a broken log collector must never break login. Batching, retries, and the endpoint
  contract are deliberately [3mnot[0m built; that's the work that gets done when you have a collector.

  [1m7. Call sites[0m

  [38;5;153mapp.js[39m: the three [38;5;153mconsole.*[39m calls become logger calls — [38;5;153minfo[39m on login attempt (username only; the password never
  enters a log call), [38;5;153minfo[39m on result, [38;5;153mwarn[39m on validation failure.

  [38;5;153msrc/index.js[39m: one judgment call worth flagging. [38;5;153mconsole.log(greet('world'))[39m is the program's [3moutput[0m, not a diagnostic
  — routing it through the logger would wrap the greeting in a JSON envelope and change what the program prints. I'd
  leave that line alone and add [38;5;153mlogger.debug[39m around [38;5;153mmain()[39m start/finish instead.

  [1m8. Tests — [38;5;153mtest/logger.test.js[39m, [38;5;153mnode --test[0m

  Adds [38;5;153m"scripts": {"test": "node --test"}[39m to [38;5;153mpackage.json[39m; no dependencies. Covers: level filtering, redaction (nested,
  arrays, mixed case, no caller mutation), sink receives the redacted record, a throwing sink doesn't propagate, record
  shape, and cycle/depth safety.

  [1mFiles:[0m new [38;5;153msrc/logger.js[39m, new [38;5;153mtest/logger.test.js[39m; edits to [38;5;153mapp.js[39m, [38;5;153mindex.html[39m, [38;5;153msrc/index.js[39m, [38;5;153mpackage.json[39m.

  [1mNot included:[0m log rotation, a collector endpoint, request/correlation IDs, sampling, and any change to the
  [38;5;153mapi.example.com[39m stub.

  If this looks right, I'll write it up as a spec at [38;5;153mdocs/hyperpowers/specs/2026-09-16-shared-logging-design.md[39m
  (uncommitted, per your CLAUDE.md) and hand off to the writing-plans skill for the implementation plan. Anything you
  want changed first — particularly §7, since it's the one place I'm proposing to leave an existing [38;5;153mconsole.log[39m in
  place?

